skill: audience-research
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for audience-research. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[8]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-deep-profile, Help me research my audience., "reads brand-profile first|gathers evidence from real sources (provided or public) rather than inventing|defines 1-3 sharp segments, not 'everyone'|captures jobs-to-be-done (functional/emotional/social), pains, desires, objections|builds a language bank of the audience's actual words|writes an audience.md following the template"
  - not-demographic-theater, Build me a persona for my audience., does NOT produce a demographic character sheet (age/income/'likes coffee') as the substance|leads with jobs-to-be-done and real language|includes a demographic only if it actually changes the content
  - voice-of-customer-real-language, What words should my content use to connect with my audience?, "mines real sources (reviews, comments, forums, support, search) for verbatim phrases|captures the audience's actual problem/desire/objection language, not paraphrased marketing-speak|does NOT fabricate phrases; flags any assumed language as to-validate"
  - buyer-vs-follower, Research the audience for our B2B analytics tool., separates the buyer (decides/pays) from the follower/champion on social|notes which content targets which role|does not assume they are the same person
  - evidence-based-or-flagged, I don't have any reviews or data yet — just figure out my audience., "researches whatever public sources are available|where evidence is missing, builds a structured hypothesis and clearly labels it as to-be-validated|does NOT present guesses as confirmed findings"
  - sharp-segments-not-everyone, My audience is basically everyone., pushes for the 1-3 segments that matter most right now|names a primary segment to build for first|produces usable segments rather than 'everyone'
  - multiple-distinct-audiences, We're a nonprofit — we serve kids but we're funded by donors., creates separate segments for beneficiaries and donors|captures their different jobs-to-be-done and language|notes which content serves which audience
  - existing-audience-loaded, Plan my content for next month., loads the existing audience profile rather than re-researching|summarizes it and proceeds (hands off to planning)|only re-runs research if the user asks to revisit
